For orthonormal $bold(e_1), bold(e_2), bold(e_3)$ in $RR^3$,
$ bold(e_i) dot bold(e_j) = cases(1 quad i = j, 0 quad i != j), $
which is equivalent to choosing Cartesian axes along these directions, so ${bold(e_1), bold(e_2), bold(e_3)}$ is an orthonormal basis. Under $(bold(z), bold(w)) = sum_i overline(z_i) w_i$, the standard basis of $CC^n$ is likewise orthonormal.
